<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- Required. Presenting a camera without this is an instant crash, not a
	     denial. Localized through Resources/InfoPlist.xcstrings; this value is
	     the base, and what a device in an unlisted language sees.

	     There is deliberately no NSPhotoLibraryUsageDescription: every library
	     read in the app goes through PhotosPicker, which runs out of process
	     and hands back only what the person picked. It asks for no permission,
	     so declaring one would be claiming access the app never requests. -->
	<key>NSCameraUsageDescription</key>
	<string>So you can take a profile photo without leaving NestZone. The camera opens only when you tap Take Photo.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
